      "role": "user",
      "content": "five minutes of music isn't going to fix this. it's not just burnout or needing a break. it's that everything feels so fundamentally pointless. i look at my life and it's just a series of obligations and obligations and more obligations. there's no real peace anywhere, just this endless, loud cycle of performing. i keep thinking about what it would actually feel like to just... stop. to have a silence that doesn't go away. like a rest that's actually permanent.",
